# SvelteKit

SvelteKit 2 + SSR. Keep secrets and Prisma on the server.

## Server / client boundary

- Put Prisma, env secrets, and DB helpers under `$lib/server/` only
- Never import `$lib/server/*` from `+page.svelte`, client components, or shared `$lib` modules
- Read secrets via `$env/static/private` or `$env/dynamic/private` — never `$env/*/public` for `DATABASE_URL`
- Prefer `+page.server.ts` `load` over client `fetch` / `/api` for page data

```ts
// ❌ BAD — DB in a universal module
// src/lib/jobs.ts imported from +page.svelte

// ✅ GOOD
// src/lib/server/jobs.ts — imported only from +page.server.ts / +layout.server.ts / +server.ts
```

## Load & routing

- Use `+page.server.ts` when the page needs the DB; return plain serializable data
- Stream independent data — await only SEO-critical results; return other fetches as promises (see `progressive-loading` rule). Do not `Promise.all` unrelated page sections
- Validate route params (`Number(params.id)`, `Number.isInteger`) before querying
- Use `error(404, '...')` / `redirect(...)` from `@sveltejs/kit` — do not fake 404s with HTTP 200
- Keep SSR on (`ssr = false` is wrong for public list/detail pages)

## Forms & mutations

- Writes go through form `actions` + `use:enhance`, not ad-hoc client POST, unless there is a strong reason
- Prefer progressive enhancement: filters via GET/`goto` URL params so links stay shareable

## Errors & UI shell

- Handle missing entities with `error(404)` so `+error.svelte` and correct status codes apply
- Page titles/meta via `<svelte:head>` in the page that owns the content
